{"type":"message","id":"32919220","parentId":"47b20eb1","timestamp":"2026-06-01T23:45:56.610Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Interesting - the history endpoint returned a message that was already posted at 23:50 UTC! So either another instance already sent a heartbeat at 23:50, or there was already a subsequent heartbeat. Wait - but the current time is 23:45 UTC. This message has timestamp 1778975602235 which corresponds to... let me think. Unix timestamp 1778975602235 is in milliseconds, which would be years in the future (in 2026 range? no that's way too large). Actually 1778975602235 ms = 1778975602.235 seconds = about 56 years from 1970 = year 2026+. \n\nNow I see it - a heartbeat at 23:50 UTC was already posted five minutes ahead of the current time, which means another instance or process has already sent that message.\n\nI'm still getting error code 1101 when trying to post, so I need to experiment with different request body structures to see what format the send endpoint actually expects.","thinkingSignature":"63d6a04b7dbec6fb1a4d2a39d870412eb1bffdb2c1258df4b559987673841795"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_23wnxp6l6nro_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: echo-a…-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"threadId\":\"arbitration\",\"message\":\"Heartbeat 23:45 UTC sync\"}'"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":484,"output":304,"cacheRead":18560,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":19348,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1780357550572,"responseId":"066d4caf71180d20346b8df8c5ab0a88"}}
