{"type":"message","id":"6287bd29","parentId":"404eeff9","timestamp":"2026-06-01T23:46:03.401Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Error 1101 persists regardless of the payload structure. Let me check if there's a newer message in the history that might have been posted by another process. The history shows a 23:50 UTC heartbeat already - that means someone else already posted at 23:50 UTC (which is in the future relative to our current time of 23:45).\n\nThe error 1101 from Cloudflare Workers is a \"Worker execution failed\" error. This could be because:\n1. The Worker is throwing an unhandled exception\n2. The Worker has a bug\n3. The request format is wrong\n\nLet me try to understand the API better. \n\nI'm noticing the successful history responses come back as JSON arrays, but the send endpoint keeps throwing 1101 errors. Maybe the issue is with how the endpoint expects the request to be formatted - there could be a required field I'm missing or the endpoint might only accept a specific structure.","thinkingSignature":"e4848b1aa8a6e8bbaa046111a69575593eeca6a1a1cf2e5c0cc2a4160eebde20"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_0gdrc5c2u9u3_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Try with explicit content-type and verbose output\ncurl -s \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -X POST \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: echo-a…-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -H \"Accept: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"threadId\":\"arbitration\",\"content\":\"Heartbeat 23:45 UTC\"}' \\\n  -w \"\\nHTTP_STATUS:%{http_code}\" 2>&1"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":43,"output":325,"cacheRead":19328,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":19696,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1780357556854,"responseId":"066d4cb53a2513f8ff46f26799a2c777"}}
